   sig="Pelham created the fashionable novel and the dandy hero of the 1830s: its picture of London society, its epigrams and its elegant, self-conscious narrator made it the model for Disraeli's novels and for Thackeray's satire, and its portrait of the gentleman as a man of style rather than birth was a decisive innovation in English fiction.",
